# This repo is public -- rangdhanuduet.live is served straight out of it, and a
# custom domain on GitHub Pages means it cannot be private. So the rule here is
# the other way round from a normal project: nothing is tracked unless it is a
# file the live site actually serves.
#
# That keeps out, by default and forever:
#   backend/*.gs, backend/CODE-REVIEW-FIXES.md  -- carry the Google Sheet and
#       Drive folder IDs (13 of them). Not secrets on their own, but no reason
#       to hand them out.
#   DEPLOY-NOTES.md, CLAUDE.md, NEXT-BATCH-TAILWIND.md, REUNION-ALBUM-ORDER.md,
#       SHIFT-TO-CODE.md, RUN-THIS.txt  -- internal notes
#   test_*.js, verify.js, check*.js, rd_source.js, apply_*.py, split.js, src.css,
#       tailwind.config.js, package*.json, node_modules/  -- the toolchain
#   index.html.before-split, ORIGINAL-compare.html, outputs/, work/  -- archives
#
# A new scratch file therefore can never leak by accident: it is ignored until
# someone adds it to the allow-list below on purpose.

# 1. ignore everything, at every depth
/*

# 2. then allow back exactly what ships
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!CNAME
!index.html
!organization.html
!pdacc.html
!llms.txt
!style.css
!custom.css
!script.js
!logo.png
!pdacc-logo.png
# The DUET crest beside the brand mark in the header (brand-duet-crest in
# index.html names it), so it has to ship.
!duet-logo.png
!slide-home.jpg
!slide-pdacc.jpg
# The Association's own cover, behind every member who has not uploaded one.
# RD_MP_COVER_DEFAULT in script.js names it, so it has to ship.
!cover-default.jpg
!robots.txt
!sitemap.xml
!PROJECT_STATUS.md
!PROJECT_HANDOVER_PROMPT.md
!CODEBASE_INDEX.md
